    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, we're working on our internal documentation for the Estonia office. Can you give me a quick summary of the specific steps a company is required to take when a user submits a \"Right to be Forgotten\" request under GDPR?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely! Under GDPR, when a user submits a \"Right to be Forgotten\" request, the company should:\n\n\n1. Acknowledge the request promptly and begin assessing its validity against the GDPR criteria.\n\n2. Erase the personal data from all their systems, ensuring that backups and other copies are also deleted.\n\n3. Communicate with relevant parties who may have processed the data and confirm deletion from their systems as well.\n\n4. Ensure proper documentation of the process for legal and audit purposes.\n\n5. Confirm to the user that their personal data has been erased and update the deletion logs for accountability.",
