      "content": "To handle data in legacy systems or less accessible sub-databases in response to a \"Right to be Forgotten\" request, the following steps should be taken:\n\n\n1. Conduct a thorough search to identify all instances where the subject’s personal data might be stored.\n\n2. If certain data is elusive, request a formal search permit and assistance from GDPR authorities when necessary.\n\n3. Document the efforts taken to find and erase all necessary personal data for transparency and legal compliance.\n\n4. Notify the user of the extended efforts and maintain an open dialogue, updating them on the progress.\n\n5. Continue the search until absolutely confident that no remnants exist and inform the user once the process is complete. It's crucial to approach this with diligence, documenting every step to demonstrate the company's commitment to the regulation.",
